---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import tools from '../content/reference/mcp-tools.json';

interface Prop { type?: string; items?: { type?: string }; minimum?: number; maximum?: number; maxItems?: number; pattern?: string }
const typeOf = (p: Prop) => (p.type === 'array' ? `${p.items?.type ?? 'any'}[]` : (p.type ?? 'any'));
const notes = (p: Prop) =>
  [
    p.minimum !== undefined && `min ${p.minimum}`,
    p.maximum !== undefined && `max ${p.maximum}`,
    p.maxItems !== undefined && `at most ${p.maxItems} items`,
    p.pattern && (p.pattern === '^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$' ? 'YYYY-MM-DD' : `pattern ${p.pattern}`),
  ].filter(Boolean).join(', ');
const params = (t: (typeof tools)[number]) => {
  const schema = t.input_schema as { properties: Record<string, Prop>; required?: string[] };
  return Object.entries(schema.properties).map(([name, p]) => ({ name, type: typeOf(p), required: !!schema.required?.includes(name), notes: notes(p) }));
};
---

<Base title="Agents · velo">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Agents (MCP)</h1>
    <p>
      velo can act as an MCP server, so Claude Code (or any MCP client) can search, read, create and edit your notes.
      It is off by default.
    </p>

    <h2 id="setup">Setup</h2>
    <p>
      Turn on <strong>Agent access (MCP)</strong> in Settings › General and save. Reopen Settings and press
      <strong>Copy setup command</strong>; it holds the exact path of your install. It runs:
    </p>
    <pre><code>claude mcp add velo -- &lt;path to velo&gt; --mcp</code></pre>
    <p>Typical paths:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>macOS: <code>/Applications/velo.app/Contents/MacOS/velo</code></li>
      <li>Linux: where your package put the binary, for example <code>/usr/bin/velo</code> for the .deb</li>
      <li>Windows: not supported yet</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The client starts <code>velo --mcp</code> itself, with no window. If velo is running, the request is forwarded
      to the app; otherwise velo reads and writes the notes folder directly. The switch is checked on every call.
    </p>

    <h2 id="other-clients">Other clients</h2>
    <p>Any client that launches an MCP server over stdio works with this entry:</p>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "velo": {
      "command": "/Applications/velo.app/Contents/MacOS/velo",
      "args": ["--mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

    <h2 id="safety">Safety</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Locked notes are never listed, searched or returned, and the agent never decrypts anything.</li>
      <li>Deletes go to the Trash. There is no permanent delete.</li>
      <li>Edits are anchored (<code>old_text</code> must match once) or hash-guarded (<code>replace_note</code> fails if the note changed since you read it).</li>
      <li>A note open in velo is edited through the editor, so nothing is overwritten behind it. If velo does not take the change within 5 seconds the call fails with "velo is busy, retry" and nothing changes.</li>
      <li>Off by default. The running app listens on 127.0.0.1 only, and every request needs a random token.</li>
      <li>Every write needs a summary. velo saves a revision of the note first, marked as an agent change in the info panel; select it and press Restore.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="tools">Tools ({tools.length})</h2>
    {tools.map((t) => (
      <section class="tool" id={t.name}>
        <h3><a href={`#${t.name}`}><code>{t.name}</code></a></h3>
        <p>{t.description}</p>
        {params(t).length === 0
          ? <p><em>No parameters.</em></p>
          : (
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {params(t).map((p) => (
                  <tr><td><code>{p.name}</code></td><td>{p.type}</td><td>{p.required ? 'yes' : 'no'}</td><td>{p.notes}</td></tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          )}
      </section>
    ))}
    <p><small>Generated from the tool specs in the app (<code>src-tauri/src/agent/tools.rs</code>).</small></p>
  </article>
</Base>
